WEBVTT

00:38:56.417 --> 00:39:00.018
As the kid who was always afraid
of being called to the principal's office,

00:39:00.042 --> 00:39:02.226
that's very much the dread.

00:39:02.250 --> 00:39:05.226
I think the nonconfrontational
stance also though

00:39:05.250 --> 00:39:09.143
is not just a fear
of incurring the wrath of others.

00:39:09.167 --> 00:39:11.601
It's also a fear
of damaging the relationship

00:39:11.625 --> 00:39:12.893
and thinking about,

00:39:12.917 --> 00:39:15.559
"OK, if I can just make this person
happy in the moment,

00:39:15.583 --> 00:39:19.434
then maybe the relationship
won't be broken as a result."

00:39:19.458 --> 00:39:23.268
EP: But that means that you are the one
who carries the anxiety

00:39:23.292 --> 00:39:25.351
over the loss of the relationship,

00:39:25.375 --> 00:39:28.226
as if you're the only one
who cares about that relationship.

00:39:28.250 --> 00:39:31.768
And that's not, you know,
that is also back to the power thing.